Release 2.7.0.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 20:09:22

Added. Power button, under When the TV turns off and on: the board's power button puts the TV in standby and the
board to sleep, and the next press wakes both and switches the TV to the board. Checking it asks for your password
once. It installs a system service that makes the light bar breathe orange, turns the CPU boost off and picks a
power-saving profile around every sleep, and stops the login screen from powering the board off on a press. The
app's background service reads the button, so your user joins the input group. While it is on, cecd's own TV on and
off with sleep is off. Without sleep in the kernel, the button turns the TV off with the screen. The app now changes
the board, so the portal asks before it opens.

